# A here-document in a pipeline: `cat <<EOF | grep x` opens a heredoc on the first
# pipeline stage; the body follows the whole pipeline's terminating newline. The
# HeredocRedirect is inside the first Pipeline stage; the body drains once.
<<<cmd
printf 'cat <<EOF | grep x\nx\nEOF\n' | "$PP" run std.shell --input - --dump-tree
<<<assert
exit 0
out-absent ERROR
out-absent MISSING
out-contains Pipeline
out-count 1 HeredocRedirect
out-count 1 HeredocBody [
